1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,760
Okay, next section deals with the restrictive diseases.

2
00:00:03,060 --> 00:00:07,540
Now, I realize that this can be a particularly difficult topic,

3
00:00:07,620 --> 00:00:09,040
or quote-unquote a difficult topic,

4
00:00:09,120 --> 00:00:11,960
and medical students are a little bit wary of this topic

5
00:00:11,960 --> 00:00:14,580
because it's sort of hyped up to be particularly difficult.

6
00:00:15,080 --> 00:00:17,400
But I actually don't think that this section is that hard,

7
00:00:17,600 --> 00:00:19,320
and I'm hopeful that you'll agree with me

8
00:00:19,320 --> 00:00:21,060
by the time we reach the end of the section.

9
00:00:21,600 --> 00:00:23,540
So the first principle that you have to keep in mind

10
00:00:23,540 --> 00:00:24,840
is that in a restrictive disease,

11
00:00:25,020 --> 00:00:27,040
you're restricted from filling the lung.

12
00:00:27,040 --> 00:00:29,480
There's a problem with the ability to fill the lung.

13
00:00:29,480 --> 00:00:31,500
Now, remember that in an obstructive disease,

14
00:00:31,620 --> 00:00:33,660
the problem was the ability to empty the lung.

15
00:00:34,080 --> 00:00:37,400
In a restrictive disease, the problem is the ability to fill the lung.

16
00:00:37,840 --> 00:00:39,000
If you can't fill the lung,

17
00:00:39,120 --> 00:00:41,400
obviously the total lung capacity is going to go down.

18
00:00:41,540 --> 00:00:43,800
If you can't bring air into the lung,

19
00:00:44,180 --> 00:00:46,440
the total lung capacity measures how much air

20
00:00:46,440 --> 00:00:47,600
you can actually hold in the lung.

21
00:00:47,640 --> 00:00:49,040
And if you can't put air in the lung,

22
00:00:49,280 --> 00:00:51,540
obviously the total lung capacity will be down.

23
00:00:52,360 --> 00:00:54,960
In addition, the forced vital capacity will be down.

24
00:00:55,340 --> 00:00:57,160
The forced vital capacity is the amount of air

25
00:00:57,160 --> 00:01:00,100
that you can blow out after breathing in all the way.

26
00:01:00,220 --> 00:01:01,420
So you take a very deep breath

27
00:01:01,420 --> 00:01:02,780
and blow out as much as you can.

28
00:01:03,120 --> 00:01:05,240
That's the forced vital capacity.

29
00:01:05,440 --> 00:01:06,160
And that will be down

30
00:01:06,160 --> 00:01:07,780
because if you can't bring air into the lung,

31
00:01:07,840 --> 00:01:08,620
you're going to have a problem.

32
00:01:09,080 --> 00:01:11,440
You're not going to be able to get that much air out, right?

33
00:01:11,500 --> 00:01:12,400
So that you can't fill it,

34
00:01:12,460 --> 00:01:13,900
so therefore there'll be less coming out.

35
00:01:14,240 --> 00:01:16,320
So the forced vital capacity will be down.

36
00:01:16,820 --> 00:01:19,440
The forced expiratory volume over a one-second period,

37
00:01:19,580 --> 00:01:21,200
the FEV1, will also be down.

38
00:01:21,620 --> 00:01:23,140
And that, again, is the amount of air

39
00:01:23,140 --> 00:01:24,760
that comes out in the first second

40
00:01:24,760 --> 00:01:27,280
after you breathe all the way in and then blow out.

41
00:01:27,360 --> 00:01:29,380
So when you're blowing out that very first second,

42
00:01:29,600 --> 00:01:32,240
that's the amount of air that comes out in that first second.

43
00:01:32,340 --> 00:01:33,900
And if you can't fill the lung,

44
00:01:33,980 --> 00:01:35,700
you're not going to be able to get as much air out

45
00:01:35,700 --> 00:01:36,860
in that first second period.

46
00:01:37,760 --> 00:01:39,160
What's important to note, however,

47
00:01:39,160 --> 00:01:40,300
is that this ratio,

48
00:01:40,580 --> 00:01:43,220
again, both the FEV1 and the FVC are going down,

49
00:01:43,520 --> 00:01:46,440
but the ratio actually increases.

50
00:01:47,380 --> 00:01:48,520
Now, what do I mean by that?

51
00:01:48,560 --> 00:01:49,840
Let's go back to normal for a minute.

52
00:01:50,200 --> 00:01:53,020
Remember that the normal forced expiratory volume

53
00:01:53,020 --> 00:01:54,980
over a one-second period is four liters.

54
00:01:55,360 --> 00:01:58,240
So that when I breathe in all the way and I blow out,

55
00:01:58,320 --> 00:02:00,680
in the first second, I'm going to blow out about four liters.

56
00:02:01,160 --> 00:02:02,820
And the total amount that I can blow out,

57
00:02:02,940 --> 00:02:05,840
the forced vital capacity, would be about five liters.

58
00:02:05,940 --> 00:02:09,920
So otherwise stated, normally about 80% of the air

59
00:02:09,920 --> 00:02:12,120
is blown out in the first second.

60
00:02:12,960 --> 00:02:15,480
Now, what happens in a restrictive disease

61
00:02:15,480 --> 00:02:18,760
is that my forced vital capacity,

62
00:02:18,920 --> 00:02:20,500
the amount of air that I can blow out totally,

63
00:02:20,620 --> 00:02:21,340
would go down.

64
00:02:21,420 --> 00:02:23,880
So for example, let's say that that goes down to four liters.

65
00:02:24,480 --> 00:02:26,080
And my forced expiratory volume,

66
00:02:26,200 --> 00:02:27,820
the amount that's going to come out in that first second,

67
00:02:27,900 --> 00:02:28,840
is also going to go down,

68
00:02:28,920 --> 00:02:31,340
but it's not going to go down as much relative to normal.

69
00:02:31,560 --> 00:02:33,880
So that maybe it becomes 3.5.

70
00:02:33,880 --> 00:02:38,120
So when, you know, 3.5 over four is like greater than 85%.

71
00:02:38,120 --> 00:02:41,760
So this becomes greater than 80%.

72
00:02:41,760 --> 00:02:45,100
And that's important because that's one of the classic hallmarks

73
00:02:45,100 --> 00:02:47,640
of this particular, these particular disorders.

74
00:02:47,940 --> 00:02:49,280
And it's pretty easy to remember

75
00:02:49,280 --> 00:02:52,820
because basically that forced expiratory volume over one second,

76
00:02:52,960 --> 00:02:56,480
what increases it is the fact that when you get a restrictive disease,

77
00:02:56,480 --> 00:02:58,700
you often have a lot of fibrosis in the lung.

78
00:02:59,080 --> 00:03:02,900
And that fibrosis in the lung increases the elastic recoil of the lung.

79
00:03:03,220 --> 00:03:05,660
And that increase in elastic recoil is going to allow you

80
00:03:05,660 --> 00:03:07,580
to be able to squeeze air out more quickly

81
00:03:07,580 --> 00:03:09,660
over that first one second period.

82
00:03:10,180 --> 00:03:11,720
And so that's one way to think about it.

83
00:03:11,740 --> 00:03:14,160
Another way to think about it is when you get all that fibrosis,

84
00:03:14,500 --> 00:03:17,240
you're not going to get collapse of any of the airways.

85
00:03:17,300 --> 00:03:19,240
And as you don't get collapse of the airways,

86
00:03:19,560 --> 00:03:22,040
then the air is going to be able to rush out of the lung more quickly.

87
00:03:22,040 --> 00:03:25,620
Because the acceleration of the air does cause some compression

88
00:03:25,620 --> 00:03:28,420
or collapsing inward of the airways.

89
00:03:28,420 --> 00:03:30,420
But that's not going to happen because the fibrosis

90
00:03:30,420 --> 00:03:32,500
is going to trap all those airways open.

91
00:03:33,100 --> 00:03:34,780
So that's another way to think about it.

92
00:03:35,160 --> 00:03:37,540
Regardless, you do need to know that that ratio is increased.

93
00:03:37,620 --> 00:03:39,400
And remember that in the obstructive disorders,

94
00:03:39,740 --> 00:03:40,880
the ratio was decreased.

95
00:03:41,100 --> 00:03:43,640
And again, that was the hallmark of those obstructive disorders

96
00:03:43,640 --> 00:03:44,520
that we've already covered.

97
00:03:44,620 --> 00:03:47,140
You can go back and review that if that wasn't clear.

98
00:03:47,840 --> 00:03:50,200
Most commonly, the restrictive diseases

99
00:03:50,200 --> 00:03:51,700
are going to be due to something called

100
00:03:51,700 --> 00:03:53,340
an interstitial disease of the lung.

101
00:03:54,240 --> 00:03:56,000
Now, what are interstitial diseases of the lung?

102
00:03:56,000 --> 00:04:00,000
These are disorders in which you get fibrosis of the interstitium.

103
00:04:00,220 --> 00:04:01,200
And what's the interstitium?

104
00:04:01,540 --> 00:04:02,660
Well, if you go back and recall,

105
00:04:02,760 --> 00:04:04,720
remember that you've got these alveolar air sacs

106
00:04:04,720 --> 00:04:06,420
down in the exchange portion of the lung.

107
00:04:06,760 --> 00:04:08,760
And the wall of these alveolar air sacs

108
00:04:08,760 --> 00:04:10,480
is super delicate and thin.

109
00:04:10,920 --> 00:04:13,160
Now, the reason you want that to be super delicate and thin

110
00:04:13,160 --> 00:04:16,180
is because you're going to exchange oxygen and carbon dioxide

111
00:04:16,180 --> 00:04:17,120
across that barrier.

112
00:04:17,240 --> 00:04:18,680
So you want a super thin barrier.

113
00:04:19,240 --> 00:04:21,180
In an interstitial fibrosing process,

114
00:04:21,180 --> 00:04:23,980
you get fibrosis of the interstitium.

115
00:04:24,640 --> 00:04:26,260
And it's fibrosis of the interstitium

116
00:04:26,260 --> 00:04:27,520
that thickens that barrier.

117
00:04:27,780 --> 00:04:29,020
And the thickening of the barrier

118
00:04:29,020 --> 00:04:31,540
then is going to prohibit the ability

119
00:04:31,540 --> 00:04:33,240
to exchange gases very well.

120
00:04:33,320 --> 00:04:34,300
That's going to be one problem.

121
00:04:34,620 --> 00:04:36,160
But another problem is you're not going to be able

122
00:04:36,160 --> 00:04:38,120
to fill that lung because it's going to be hard

123
00:04:38,120 --> 00:04:41,300
to open that fibrosis when you want to fill this airway.

124
00:04:41,800 --> 00:04:43,100
And so there's going to be a problem.

125
00:04:43,180 --> 00:04:44,580
There's going to be a restrictive problem,

126
00:04:44,860 --> 00:04:47,280
an inability to properly fill the lung.

127
00:04:47,980 --> 00:04:50,260
So that's the most common cause of restrictive disease,

128
00:04:50,380 --> 00:04:51,640
interstitial fibrosis.

129
00:04:52,080 --> 00:04:54,080
Now, another way by which we can have

130
00:04:54,080 --> 00:04:55,320
a restricted filling of the lung

131
00:04:55,320 --> 00:04:58,180
is by having an abnormality of the chest wall.

132
00:04:58,280 --> 00:05:00,380
For example, let's say the patient's obese, right?

133
00:05:00,720 --> 00:05:02,700
So as the patient is trying to fill the lung,

134
00:05:02,800 --> 00:05:04,520
they've got to blow open that chest wall.

135
00:05:05,060 --> 00:05:06,920
They've got to fight the force of the chest

136
00:05:06,920 --> 00:05:08,460
in order to open the lung completely.

137
00:05:08,820 --> 00:05:11,040
And so if there is a lot of force in the chest wall,

138
00:05:11,120 --> 00:05:12,500
for example, due to obesity,

139
00:05:13,020 --> 00:05:15,660
that force in the chest wall is going to prohibit the lung

140
00:05:15,660 --> 00:05:18,160
from being able to open and fill as much.

141
00:05:18,540 --> 00:05:23,200
And so that would also result in a restrictive disease.

142
00:05:23,760 --> 00:05:25,000
Now, the first of these disorders

143
00:05:25,000 --> 00:05:27,580
is called idiopathic pulmonary fibrosis.

144
00:05:27,640 --> 00:05:29,080
And the key disorder here

145
00:05:29,080 --> 00:05:31,880
is that you get fibrosis of the lung interstitium.

146
00:05:32,500 --> 00:05:34,440
All right, idiopathic pulmonary fibrosis

147
00:05:34,440 --> 00:05:36,980
where you get fibrosis of the lung interstitium.

148
00:05:37,200 --> 00:05:38,820
This is what it classically looks like.

149
00:05:38,900 --> 00:05:40,000
And you can see here,

150
00:05:40,080 --> 00:05:41,480
this is probably as close to normal

151
00:05:41,480 --> 00:05:42,660
as we have on this slide.

152
00:05:42,980 --> 00:05:44,820
This is the normal alveolar air sac.

153
00:05:44,820 --> 00:05:48,260
And you can see that the wall of the alveolar sac

154
00:05:48,260 --> 00:05:50,560
is very thin and delicate.

155
00:05:51,080 --> 00:05:51,860
Now, notice here,

156
00:05:51,980 --> 00:05:53,840
you've got another alveolar air sac here,

157
00:05:54,020 --> 00:05:56,320
but this wall is way too thick.

158
00:05:56,440 --> 00:05:57,820
This interstitium has become fibrosed.

159
00:05:58,460 --> 00:05:59,960
Here, you can see how much fibrosis

160
00:05:59,960 --> 00:06:01,160
there is in the interstitium.

161
00:06:01,660 --> 00:06:03,760
And so that's classic for this disorder

162
00:06:03,760 --> 00:06:05,900
called idiopathic pulmonary fibrosis.

163
00:06:06,500 --> 00:06:07,700
Now, in this particular disorder,

164
00:06:07,820 --> 00:06:10,160
what happens is you get cyclical lung injury.

165
00:06:10,260 --> 00:06:11,340
And nobody knows why,

166
00:06:11,580 --> 00:06:12,920
hence the term idiopathic.

167
00:06:12,920 --> 00:06:14,620
But our current understanding is that

168
00:06:14,620 --> 00:06:16,080
with this cyclical lung injury,

169
00:06:16,280 --> 00:06:17,740
you get cyclical healing.

170
00:06:17,880 --> 00:06:19,960
And remember that one of the key mediators of healing

171
00:06:19,960 --> 00:06:21,380
is TGF-beta.

172
00:06:21,580 --> 00:06:23,020
If you go back and recall

173
00:06:23,020 --> 00:06:25,140
from your lectures in inflammation,

174
00:06:25,800 --> 00:06:27,280
I mentioned during inflammation

175
00:06:27,280 --> 00:06:28,960
that when the macrophages come in,

176
00:06:29,360 --> 00:06:30,960
the macrophages can do different things.

177
00:06:30,960 --> 00:06:33,400
Like they can create additional acute inflammation

178
00:06:33,400 --> 00:06:34,800
by secreting IL-8.

179
00:06:35,240 --> 00:06:36,980
They can induce fibrosis.

180
00:06:37,080 --> 00:06:39,200
They can call in the healing response.

181
00:06:39,200 --> 00:06:40,300
And at that point,

182
00:06:40,360 --> 00:06:42,520
I told you that there were two important mediators

183
00:06:42,520 --> 00:06:44,580
that allow for calling in of the healing response.

184
00:06:44,680 --> 00:06:46,140
And one was TGF-beta,

185
00:06:46,200 --> 00:06:47,560
and the other one was IL-10.

186
00:06:47,980 --> 00:06:49,420
And so in this particular case,

187
00:06:49,460 --> 00:06:51,640
you can see that TGF-beta is important

188
00:06:51,640 --> 00:06:52,900
for the healing response.

189
00:06:53,020 --> 00:06:54,460
And so the injured pneumocytes

190
00:06:54,460 --> 00:06:56,860
can also release TGF-beta,

191
00:06:56,940 --> 00:06:58,180
and that would induce fibrosis.

192
00:06:58,240 --> 00:07:01,040
And that is what is thought to drive the process.

193
00:07:01,160 --> 00:07:03,120
It's TGF-beta from the injured pneumocytes

194
00:07:03,120 --> 00:07:04,680
that induces the fibrosis.

195
00:07:05,080 --> 00:07:05,980
That's important to know.

196
00:07:06,800 --> 00:07:07,220
Now remember,

197
00:07:07,320 --> 00:07:09,500
when a patient has this kind of interstitial fibrosis,

198
00:07:09,800 --> 00:07:12,260
you have to first exclude other causes.

199
00:07:12,520 --> 00:07:13,360
So for example,

200
00:07:13,460 --> 00:07:14,140
you have to make sure

201
00:07:14,140 --> 00:07:15,620
that it's not due to some drugs,

202
00:07:15,640 --> 00:07:17,720
like bleomycin is a high-yield example,

203
00:07:18,080 --> 00:07:20,180
or amiodarum is another high-yield example.

204
00:07:20,460 --> 00:07:22,000
You've got to exclude radiation therapy,

205
00:07:22,000 --> 00:07:24,380
which can also cause an interstitial fibrosis.

206
00:07:24,380 --> 00:07:26,620
And you've got to exclude other causes as well.

207
00:07:27,020 --> 00:07:29,440
And once you've excluded all the other causes,

208
00:07:29,680 --> 00:07:32,900
then you would call it idiopathic pulmonary fibrosis.

209
00:07:33,420 --> 00:07:33,860
Now clinically,

210
00:07:34,000 --> 00:07:35,640
these patients are going to have shortness of breath

211
00:07:35,640 --> 00:07:37,080
that's going to get worse over time.

212
00:07:37,120 --> 00:07:38,200
And it gets worse over time

213
00:07:38,200 --> 00:07:40,320
because the fibrosis progresses over time.

214
00:07:40,680 --> 00:07:41,320
At the same time,

215
00:07:41,340 --> 00:07:42,140
they're going to have cough.

216
00:07:42,540 --> 00:07:43,980
If a lung CT was performed,

217
00:07:44,080 --> 00:07:45,960
you would see fibrosis on that lung CT.

218
00:07:46,460 --> 00:07:47,700
Very important to know

219
00:07:47,700 --> 00:07:50,540
is that the fibrosis initially begins

220
00:07:50,540 --> 00:07:52,280
in the sub-pleural regions,

221
00:07:52,420 --> 00:07:53,840
right underneath the pleural of the lung.

222
00:07:54,180 --> 00:07:55,540
And eventually, over time,

223
00:07:55,600 --> 00:07:57,680
it can progress to involve the entire lung.

224
00:07:58,020 --> 00:07:59,420
When it involves the entire lung

225
00:07:59,420 --> 00:08:01,480
and there's diffuse fibrosis throughout the lung,

226
00:08:01,880 --> 00:08:03,100
that's called honeycomb lung.

227
00:08:03,100 --> 00:08:05,440
Now there's no way to remove this fibrosis

228
00:08:05,440 --> 00:08:07,740
and so the treatment is lung transplantation.

229
00:08:08,060 --> 00:08:10,920
And that's because we have no way of removing the fibrosis.

230
00:08:11,640 --> 00:08:14,480
Another disorder that could result in interstitial fibrosis

231
00:08:14,480 --> 00:08:16,160
is called the pneumoconiosis.

232
00:08:16,900 --> 00:08:19,540
Pneumoconiosis are basically disorders

233
00:08:19,540 --> 00:08:20,900
in which you get fibrosis

234
00:08:20,900 --> 00:08:23,160
due to some occupational exposure

235
00:08:23,160 --> 00:08:25,240
that then activates the macrophages

236
00:08:25,240 --> 00:08:27,280
to lay down fibrosis.

237
00:08:27,600 --> 00:08:28,900
Let's start with small particles.

238
00:08:28,900 --> 00:08:31,780
Now the notion is that if you've got big particles

239
00:08:31,780 --> 00:08:32,940
present in the environment,

240
00:08:33,860 --> 00:08:34,760
when you breathe in,

241
00:08:34,880 --> 00:08:37,100
the mucus and the cilia, etc.,

242
00:08:37,100 --> 00:08:39,000
will actually filter those big particles.

243
00:08:39,500 --> 00:08:41,120
So these have to be particles

244
00:08:41,120 --> 00:08:42,040
that are small enough

245
00:08:42,040 --> 00:08:45,060
that can get to the very bottom exchange

246
00:08:45,060 --> 00:08:47,180
or distal exchange portion of the lung,

247
00:08:47,500 --> 00:08:50,300
which will then induce the fibrosis in the interstitium.

248
00:08:50,500 --> 00:08:51,160
That's point one.

249
00:08:51,700 --> 00:08:52,800
Point number two is that

250
00:08:52,800 --> 00:08:54,700
the fibrosis in the interstitium

251
00:08:54,700 --> 00:08:55,420
in these disorders

252
00:08:55,420 --> 00:08:57,200
is mediated by the macrophages.

253
00:08:57,200 --> 00:08:59,120
Basically what happens

254
00:08:59,120 --> 00:09:00,980
is these tiny particles come in,

255
00:09:01,400 --> 00:09:02,800
they get to the bottom of the lung,

256
00:09:02,940 --> 00:09:04,460
and in the very bottom of the lung,

257
00:09:04,560 --> 00:09:05,840
the distal portion of the lung,

258
00:09:06,120 --> 00:09:07,260
the only thing that you have

259
00:09:07,260 --> 00:09:08,200
to defend yourself there

260
00:09:08,200 --> 00:09:09,440
is the alveolar macrophage.

261
00:09:09,840 --> 00:09:11,800
The alveolar macrophage consumes those particles,

262
00:09:11,900 --> 00:09:12,680
and when it consumes them,

263
00:09:12,740 --> 00:09:13,060
it says,

264
00:09:13,180 --> 00:09:14,060
what the heck is this?

265
00:09:14,080 --> 00:09:15,440
I don't recognize this as anything.

266
00:09:15,840 --> 00:09:16,840
This is some foreign thing.

267
00:09:16,900 --> 00:09:18,380
I have no idea what to do with this.

268
00:09:18,800 --> 00:09:20,440
And so when it has no idea what to do with this,

269
00:09:20,460 --> 00:09:21,220
it freaks out

270
00:09:21,220 --> 00:09:23,640
and begins to start inducing fibrosis

271
00:09:23,640 --> 00:09:24,540
all over the lung,

272
00:09:24,620 --> 00:09:26,620
trying to basically wall off this garbage.

273
00:09:27,200 --> 00:09:28,880
And as it induces this fibrosis,

274
00:09:28,980 --> 00:09:29,680
that's what results

275
00:09:29,680 --> 00:09:31,180
in the interstitial fibrosis

276
00:09:31,180 --> 00:09:32,820
that you see in a pneumoconiosis.

277
00:09:33,400 --> 00:09:34,160
And that's why I say

278
00:09:34,160 --> 00:09:35,540
that the small particles have to,

279
00:09:35,840 --> 00:09:37,580
they have to be able to induce fibrosis

280
00:09:37,580 --> 00:09:38,400
by the macrophages.

281
00:09:38,540 --> 00:09:39,600
Obviously they have to be small

282
00:09:39,600 --> 00:09:40,480
because they wouldn't be able

283
00:09:40,480 --> 00:09:41,660
to get to the bottom of the lung

284
00:09:41,660 --> 00:09:42,440
if they weren't small,

285
00:09:42,800 --> 00:09:43,580
and they have to be able

286
00:09:43,580 --> 00:09:44,640
to induce fibrosis.

287
00:09:44,940 --> 00:09:46,320
Now because this is going to be

288
00:09:46,320 --> 00:09:48,080
a severe chronic disease,

289
00:09:48,760 --> 00:09:49,900
there's going to need

290
00:09:49,900 --> 00:09:51,060
to be a chronic exposure.

291
00:09:51,200 --> 00:09:52,720
If you had a little bit of fibrosis

292
00:09:52,720 --> 00:09:54,280
induced in a little area of the lung,

293
00:09:54,280 --> 00:09:55,500
that wouldn't really create

294
00:09:55,500 --> 00:09:56,360
clinical symptoms.

295
00:09:56,900 --> 00:09:58,160
So chronic exposure

296
00:09:58,160 --> 00:10:01,080
of some sort of occupational element,

297
00:10:01,540 --> 00:10:02,980
which is a small particle,

298
00:10:03,500 --> 00:10:05,200
which will then induce fibrosis,

299
00:10:05,260 --> 00:10:06,380
which is going to be mediated

300
00:10:06,380 --> 00:10:07,340
by the macrophages.

301
00:10:07,500 --> 00:10:08,780
Those are the pneumoconiosis.

302
00:10:09,280 --> 00:10:10,920
Now here are a few high yield ones,

303
00:10:10,960 --> 00:10:11,980
and I put them in a table.

304
00:10:12,360 --> 00:10:13,240
So the very first one

305
00:10:13,240 --> 00:10:15,020
is called coal workers pneumoconiosis,

306
00:10:15,180 --> 00:10:16,300
and you can refer to your book.

307
00:10:16,340 --> 00:10:17,520
It might be a little hard to see

308
00:10:17,520 --> 00:10:18,460
on the screen.

309
00:10:19,380 --> 00:10:20,280
In coal workers pneumoconiosis,

310
00:10:20,280 --> 00:10:23,440
the problem is carbon gets taken in

311
00:10:23,440 --> 00:10:24,720
as they're working in coal mines,

312
00:10:24,820 --> 00:10:25,280
for example,

313
00:10:25,640 --> 00:10:27,000
and as this carbon comes in,

314
00:10:27,060 --> 00:10:28,200
it gets into the macrophages,

315
00:10:28,260 --> 00:10:29,760
and the macrophages don't recognize

316
00:10:29,760 --> 00:10:30,580
what to do with it.

317
00:10:30,840 --> 00:10:32,400
They begin to induce fibrosis,

318
00:10:32,460 --> 00:10:34,040
and you get massive fibrosis

319
00:10:34,040 --> 00:10:34,460
of the lung.

320
00:10:34,560 --> 00:10:35,000
Now of course,

321
00:10:35,100 --> 00:10:36,960
coal workers are chronically exposed

322
00:10:36,960 --> 00:10:37,880
to this potentially.

323
00:10:38,440 --> 00:10:40,000
So that results in massive fibrosis

324
00:10:40,000 --> 00:10:40,480
of the lung,

325
00:10:40,820 --> 00:10:41,820
and that is called

326
00:10:41,820 --> 00:10:43,260
coal workers pneumoconiosis.

327
00:10:43,840 --> 00:10:44,660
Now classically,

328
00:10:44,780 --> 00:10:45,620
what that would result in

329
00:10:45,620 --> 00:10:46,940
is something called black lung,

330
00:10:47,160 --> 00:10:48,740
where the entire lung is black

331
00:10:48,740 --> 00:10:50,660
due to the presence of this coal,

332
00:10:51,120 --> 00:10:52,080
and it would result

333
00:10:52,080 --> 00:10:53,020
in a shrunken lung

334
00:10:53,020 --> 00:10:54,140
because the entire lung

335
00:10:54,140 --> 00:10:55,100
becomes fibrotic.

336
00:10:55,660 --> 00:10:56,660
One of the associations

337
00:10:56,660 --> 00:10:58,460
with coal workers pneumoconiosis

338
00:10:58,460 --> 00:10:59,420
is something called

339
00:10:59,420 --> 00:11:00,300
rheumatoid arthritis,

340
00:11:00,480 --> 00:11:01,160
which we'll talk about

341
00:11:01,160 --> 00:11:02,840
when we do your joint lectures.

342
00:11:03,280 --> 00:11:03,540
However,

343
00:11:03,660 --> 00:11:05,180
the association of rheumatoid arthritis

344
00:11:05,180 --> 00:11:06,680
with coal worker pneumoconiosis

345
00:11:06,680 --> 00:11:08,420
is also known as Kaplan,

346
00:11:08,520 --> 00:11:09,000
with a C,

347
00:11:09,180 --> 00:11:09,980
Kaplan syndrome.

348
00:11:10,740 --> 00:11:11,720
So that's an important

349
00:11:11,720 --> 00:11:13,300
pathologic consideration.

350
00:11:14,040 --> 00:11:14,860
Now let me remind you

351
00:11:14,860 --> 00:11:15,560
that all of us

352
00:11:15,560 --> 00:11:16,500
are exposed to carbon

353
00:11:16,500 --> 00:11:17,460
just by breathing in

354
00:11:17,460 --> 00:11:18,740
the pollution from the air

355
00:11:18,740 --> 00:11:19,880
if you happen to be

356
00:11:19,880 --> 00:11:20,520
in a big city.

357
00:11:21,160 --> 00:11:22,040
And mild exposure

358
00:11:22,040 --> 00:11:23,600
of carbon occurs constantly,

359
00:11:24,060 --> 00:11:25,100
especially because

360
00:11:25,100 --> 00:11:25,740
of that pollution.

361
00:11:26,060 --> 00:11:26,760
If it's mild,

362
00:11:26,880 --> 00:11:28,180
it doesn't really do anything.

363
00:11:28,660 --> 00:11:29,500
It sort of builds up

364
00:11:29,500 --> 00:11:30,280
in the macrophages,

365
00:11:30,660 --> 00:11:31,360
and so when you have

366
00:11:31,360 --> 00:11:33,280
buildup of carbon

367
00:11:33,280 --> 00:11:34,660
within the macrophages,

368
00:11:35,080 --> 00:11:36,760
that's called anthracosis,

369
00:11:36,920 --> 00:11:37,760
and examiners like you

370
00:11:37,760 --> 00:11:38,280
to know that.

371
00:11:38,600 --> 00:11:40,380
So you can have anthracosis

372
00:11:40,380 --> 00:11:41,600
within the macrophages

373
00:11:41,600 --> 00:11:42,520
of the lung

374
00:11:42,520 --> 00:11:43,660
and within the

375
00:11:43,660 --> 00:11:44,580
hyalur lymph nodes.

376
00:11:44,580 --> 00:11:47,520
Again, that is clinically

377
00:11:47,520 --> 00:11:48,660
not significant,

378
00:11:49,040 --> 00:11:50,480
but it is common

379
00:11:50,480 --> 00:11:51,660
among the vast majority

380
00:11:51,660 --> 00:11:52,140
of people

381
00:11:52,140 --> 00:11:53,060
because the vast majority

382
00:11:53,060 --> 00:11:53,880
of people are exposed

383
00:11:53,880 --> 00:11:54,700
to pollutants

384
00:11:54,700 --> 00:11:55,380
within the air.

385
00:11:55,840 --> 00:11:56,040
All right?

386
00:11:56,180 --> 00:11:57,480
So that's coal worker's

387
00:11:57,480 --> 00:11:58,080
pneumoconiosis,

388
00:11:58,300 --> 00:11:58,840
and I've also,

389
00:11:59,000 --> 00:11:59,640
in this context,

390
00:11:59,800 --> 00:12:01,080
explained anthracosis.

391
00:12:02,100 --> 00:12:04,020
The next of the pneumoconiosis

392
00:12:04,020 --> 00:12:04,940
is silicosis,

393
00:12:05,040 --> 00:12:05,820
and in silicosis,

394
00:12:05,960 --> 00:12:06,720
the idea is that

395
00:12:06,720 --> 00:12:07,880
there's exposure to silica.

396
00:12:08,360 --> 00:12:09,420
Now silica can occur

397
00:12:09,420 --> 00:12:10,360
if the patient's

398
00:12:10,360 --> 00:12:11,120
a silica minor.

399
00:12:11,460 --> 00:12:12,320
It occurs, for example,

400
00:12:12,320 --> 00:12:13,300
in sandblasters,

401
00:12:13,420 --> 00:12:14,480
there's silica in sand,

402
00:12:14,540 --> 00:12:15,220
and sandblasters

403
00:12:15,220 --> 00:12:16,380
are people that take sand

404
00:12:16,380 --> 00:12:18,320
and shoot it at brick

405
00:12:18,320 --> 00:12:19,880
at a very, very high pressure

406
00:12:19,880 --> 00:12:20,740
with the idea

407
00:12:20,740 --> 00:12:22,020
that the friction created

408
00:12:22,020 --> 00:12:23,000
by the shooting of sand

409
00:12:23,000 --> 00:12:23,460
against brick

410
00:12:23,460 --> 00:12:24,760
will actually clean the brick,

411
00:12:24,840 --> 00:12:25,520
so it's a mechanism

412
00:12:25,520 --> 00:12:26,640
used to clean

413
00:12:26,640 --> 00:12:27,980
the surface of buildings,

414
00:12:28,440 --> 00:12:29,820
and so a sandblaster,

415
00:12:29,940 --> 00:12:30,400
quote-unquote,

416
00:12:30,640 --> 00:12:31,560
could actually get exposed

417
00:12:31,560 --> 00:12:32,560
to silica as well.

418
00:12:33,020 --> 00:12:34,020
Now one important thing

419
00:12:34,020 --> 00:12:34,540
about silica,

420
00:12:34,620 --> 00:12:35,260
if you remember this,

421
00:12:35,300 --> 00:12:35,680
you're done,

422
00:12:36,020 --> 00:12:36,620
and that is that

423
00:12:36,620 --> 00:12:37,360
when silica gets

424
00:12:37,360 --> 00:12:38,220
into macrophages,

425
00:12:38,580 --> 00:12:39,380
it impairs

426
00:12:39,380 --> 00:12:40,780
the phagolysosomes

427
00:12:40,780 --> 00:12:41,340
to form.

428
00:12:41,340 --> 00:12:43,240
The phagosome

429
00:12:43,240 --> 00:12:44,160
is the vesicle

430
00:12:44,160 --> 00:12:44,860
that's generated

431
00:12:44,860 --> 00:12:45,620
when macrophages

432
00:12:45,620 --> 00:12:46,620
eat to kill something,

433
00:12:47,020 --> 00:12:47,740
and the lysosome

434
00:12:47,740 --> 00:12:49,100
is where the phagosome

435
00:12:49,100 --> 00:12:49,980
merges in order

436
00:12:49,980 --> 00:12:50,380
to be able

437
00:12:50,380 --> 00:12:51,340
to destroy that thing.

438
00:12:51,760 --> 00:12:52,520
So what happens

439
00:12:52,520 --> 00:12:53,280
in this particular

440
00:12:53,280 --> 00:12:55,680
situation of silicosis

441
00:12:55,680 --> 00:12:57,060
is that the silica

442
00:12:57,060 --> 00:12:58,180
gets into the macrophages

443
00:12:58,180 --> 00:12:59,540
and impairs the formation

444
00:12:59,540 --> 00:13:00,840
of the phagolysosomes.

445
00:13:01,200 --> 00:13:01,960
Why is that important?

446
00:13:02,300 --> 00:13:03,460
Because it's the only

447
00:13:03,460 --> 00:13:04,680
pneumoconiosis,

448
00:13:04,840 --> 00:13:05,400
and this is the

449
00:13:05,400 --> 00:13:06,100
high-yield point.

450
00:13:06,400 --> 00:13:07,200
It is the only

451
00:13:07,200 --> 00:13:07,940
pneumoconiosis

452
00:13:07,940 --> 00:13:08,540
that increases

453
00:13:08,540 --> 00:13:09,360
your risk for TB.

454
00:13:09,360 --> 00:13:10,920
Now, once you know

455
00:13:10,920 --> 00:13:11,460
that it increases

456
00:13:11,460 --> 00:13:12,140
your risk for TB,

457
00:13:12,260 --> 00:13:12,700
then you're also

458
00:13:12,700 --> 00:13:13,120
going to know

459
00:13:13,120 --> 00:13:14,200
where it commonly

460
00:13:14,200 --> 00:13:16,340
occurs within the lung,

461
00:13:16,700 --> 00:13:17,420
and it results

462
00:13:17,420 --> 00:13:18,560
in fibrotic nodules

463
00:13:18,560 --> 00:13:19,480
usually in the upper

464
00:13:19,480 --> 00:13:20,220
lobe of the lung.

465
00:13:20,700 --> 00:13:22,460
So I use silicosis

466
00:13:22,460 --> 00:13:23,540
and its relationship

467
00:13:23,540 --> 00:13:24,040
with TB

468
00:13:24,040 --> 00:13:25,300
to also remind me

469
00:13:25,300 --> 00:13:26,440
that these patients

470
00:13:26,440 --> 00:13:26,940
are going to have

471
00:13:26,940 --> 00:13:28,260
fibrotic nodules

472
00:13:28,260 --> 00:13:29,220
in the upper lobe

473
00:13:29,220 --> 00:13:29,740
of the lung.

474
00:13:30,220 --> 00:13:31,000
The next of the

475
00:13:31,000 --> 00:13:32,180
pneumoconiosis

476
00:13:32,180 --> 00:13:33,520
is beryllium,

477
00:13:33,960 --> 00:13:34,680
and beryllium

478
00:13:34,680 --> 00:13:35,820
can be seen in miners.

479
00:13:36,020 --> 00:13:36,800
It can also be seen

480
00:13:36,800 --> 00:13:37,260
in workers

481
00:13:37,260 --> 00:13:38,840
in the aerospace industry.

482
00:13:39,400 --> 00:13:40,080
Now, the idea

483
00:13:40,080 --> 00:13:40,840
with beryllium

484
00:13:40,840 --> 00:13:41,960
is that it results

485
00:13:41,960 --> 00:13:43,500
in non-caseating granulomas

486
00:13:43,500 --> 00:13:44,220
in the lung,

487
00:13:44,680 --> 00:13:45,780
in the hyalur lymph nodes,

488
00:13:46,160 --> 00:13:47,400
and in other parts

489
00:13:47,400 --> 00:13:47,860
of the body,

490
00:13:47,940 --> 00:13:49,160
in other systemic organs.

491
00:13:49,720 --> 00:13:50,200
Now, guess what

492
00:13:50,200 --> 00:13:50,940
that sounds like?

493
00:13:51,020 --> 00:13:52,400
Non-caseating granulomas

494
00:13:52,400 --> 00:13:53,040
in the lung,

495
00:13:53,600 --> 00:13:54,600
in the hyalur lymph nodes,

496
00:13:54,840 --> 00:13:55,820
and systemic organs.

497
00:13:56,220 --> 00:13:57,040
Sounds exactly

498
00:13:57,040 --> 00:13:58,100
like sarcoidosis,

499
00:13:58,100 --> 00:13:59,240
and it is kind of

500
00:13:59,240 --> 00:13:59,920
very similar

501
00:13:59,920 --> 00:14:00,980
to sarcoidosis.

502
00:14:01,080 --> 00:14:01,420
However,

503
00:14:01,820 --> 00:14:02,960
in this particular case,

504
00:14:03,220 --> 00:14:03,860
this is driven

505
00:14:03,860 --> 00:14:04,640
by beryllium.

506
00:14:05,100 --> 00:14:06,060
So this is what I call

507
00:14:06,060 --> 00:14:07,300
the knee-jerk questions

508
00:14:07,300 --> 00:14:08,600
on examinations,

509
00:14:08,720 --> 00:14:09,560
where they give you

510
00:14:09,560 --> 00:14:10,440
a classic history,

511
00:14:11,240 --> 00:14:11,960
and you think

512
00:14:11,960 --> 00:14:12,640
that this is just

513
00:14:12,640 --> 00:14:13,920
sort of a slam-dunk question,

514
00:14:14,200 --> 00:14:14,920
and so you quickly

515
00:14:14,920 --> 00:14:15,980
pick sarcoidosis,

516
00:14:16,060 --> 00:14:16,700
but actually they were

517
00:14:16,700 --> 00:14:17,580
hinting at beryllium.

518
00:14:17,920 --> 00:14:18,560
So if they tell you

519
00:14:18,560 --> 00:14:19,080
that the patient

520
00:14:19,080 --> 00:14:19,980
works for NASA

521
00:14:19,980 --> 00:14:21,600
or recently designed

522
00:14:21,600 --> 00:14:22,360
some sort of

523
00:14:22,360 --> 00:14:23,420
stealth fighter

524
00:14:23,420 --> 00:14:24,440
or something like that,

525
00:14:24,800 --> 00:14:25,620
then that would be

526
00:14:25,620 --> 00:14:26,260
a hint to you

527
00:14:26,260 --> 00:14:26,920
that maybe they're

528
00:14:26,920 --> 00:14:28,040
in the aerospace industry,

529
00:14:28,100 --> 00:14:28,840
and so you want

530
00:14:28,840 --> 00:14:29,520
to think twice

531
00:14:29,520 --> 00:14:30,480
about beryllium.

532
00:14:30,980 --> 00:14:31,800
Another important thing

533
00:14:31,800 --> 00:14:32,420
about beryllium,

534
00:14:32,560 --> 00:14:33,540
it increases the risk

535
00:14:33,540 --> 00:14:34,380
for lung cancer.

536
00:14:34,740 --> 00:14:35,320
But I would say

537
00:14:35,320 --> 00:14:35,960
the highest yield

538
00:14:35,960 --> 00:14:36,500
is that you get

539
00:14:36,500 --> 00:14:37,480
these non-caseating

540
00:14:37,480 --> 00:14:38,660
granulomas in the lung,

541
00:14:38,900 --> 00:14:39,920
in the hyalur lymph nodes,

542
00:14:40,200 --> 00:14:41,320
and in other organs.

543
00:14:41,800 --> 00:14:43,660
The final pneumoconiosis

544
00:14:43,660 --> 00:14:44,700
that we want to discuss

545
00:14:44,700 --> 00:14:45,580
is asbestos.

546
00:14:45,660 --> 00:14:46,600
Now asbestos fibers

547
00:14:46,600 --> 00:14:47,160
would be seen

548
00:14:47,160 --> 00:14:48,320
in people who are

549
00:14:48,320 --> 00:14:50,340
classically construction workers.

550
00:14:50,460 --> 00:14:51,420
It was used in construction

551
00:14:51,420 --> 00:14:52,100
at one time.

552
00:14:52,620 --> 00:14:52,940
Plumbers,

553
00:14:53,080 --> 00:14:54,240
it was classically used

554
00:14:54,240 --> 00:14:54,860
at one time

555
00:14:54,860 --> 00:14:56,820
to insulate pipes

556
00:14:56,820 --> 00:14:58,300
and shipyard workers

557
00:14:58,300 --> 00:14:59,280
where there used

558
00:14:59,280 --> 00:15:00,360
to be a classic exposure

559
00:15:00,360 --> 00:15:00,860
as well.

560
00:15:01,340 --> 00:15:02,440
Now in each of these cases,

561
00:15:02,580 --> 00:15:03,200
the patient would get

562
00:15:03,200 --> 00:15:04,520
exposed to asbestos fibers

563
00:15:04,520 --> 00:15:05,200
and what's important

564
00:15:05,200 --> 00:15:05,680
to know

565
00:15:05,680 --> 00:15:07,200
is asbestos does

566
00:15:07,200 --> 00:15:08,000
a couple things.

567
00:15:08,440 --> 00:15:10,080
It creates fibrosis

568
00:15:10,080 --> 00:15:10,580
in the lung

569
00:15:10,580 --> 00:15:12,160
or fibrosis in the pleura

570
00:15:12,160 --> 00:15:14,020
or cancer in the lung

571
00:15:14,020 --> 00:15:15,340
or cancer in the pleura.

572
00:15:15,740 --> 00:15:16,760
That's my little way

573
00:15:16,760 --> 00:15:17,380
of remembering this.

574
00:15:17,480 --> 00:15:18,460
Fibrosis of the lung,

575
00:15:18,600 --> 00:15:19,680
fibrosis of the pleura,

576
00:15:20,120 --> 00:15:21,040
cancer of the lung,

577
00:15:21,260 --> 00:15:22,080
cancer of the pleura.

578
00:15:22,660 --> 00:15:23,560
So if you get

579
00:15:23,560 --> 00:15:25,340
cancer of the lung,

580
00:15:25,520 --> 00:15:26,280
that's the standard

581
00:15:26,280 --> 00:15:26,960
lung cancer

582
00:15:26,960 --> 00:15:27,860
and it can also cause

583
00:15:27,860 --> 00:15:28,740
cancer of the pleura

584
00:15:28,740 --> 00:15:29,460
and remember that

585
00:15:29,460 --> 00:15:30,300
cancer of the pleura

586
00:15:30,300 --> 00:15:31,520
is called mesothelioma.

587
00:15:32,000 --> 00:15:32,880
Now there is a high yield

588
00:15:32,880 --> 00:15:33,340
association

589
00:15:33,340 --> 00:15:34,400
which I've already talked

590
00:15:34,400 --> 00:15:34,900
about in your

591
00:15:34,900 --> 00:15:35,780
neoplasia lectures

592
00:15:35,780 --> 00:15:36,980
and that is patients

593
00:15:36,980 --> 00:15:37,660
who are exposed

594
00:15:37,660 --> 00:15:38,420
to asbestos

595
00:15:38,420 --> 00:15:39,900
are much more likely

596
00:15:39,900 --> 00:15:41,040
to get lung cancer,

597
00:15:41,460 --> 00:15:42,280
much more likely

598
00:15:42,280 --> 00:15:43,180
to get lung cancer

599
00:15:43,180 --> 00:15:43,960
than they are

600
00:15:43,960 --> 00:15:45,560
to get mesothelioma

601
00:15:45,560 --> 00:15:46,920
and I've written that here

602
00:15:46,920 --> 00:15:48,060
just to remind you

603
00:15:48,060 --> 00:15:49,420
because it is so high yield.

604
00:15:50,040 --> 00:15:50,820
When patients have

605
00:15:50,820 --> 00:15:51,960
exposure to asbestos,

606
00:15:52,080 --> 00:15:53,600
it requires a confirmation

607
00:15:53,600 --> 00:15:54,480
and the way by which

608
00:15:54,480 --> 00:15:55,500
we can make that confirmation

609
00:15:55,500 --> 00:15:56,900
is we can pathologically

610
00:15:56,900 --> 00:15:57,720
look for something

611
00:15:57,720 --> 00:15:59,600
called asbestos bodies

612
00:15:59,600 --> 00:16:01,180
and asbestos bodies

613
00:16:01,180 --> 00:16:02,740
basically look like this.

614
00:16:03,080 --> 00:16:04,400
You get this long

615
00:16:04,400 --> 00:16:06,520
rod shaped particle

616
00:16:06,520 --> 00:16:08,400
which classically

617
00:16:08,400 --> 00:16:10,860
has little brown beads on it

618
00:16:10,860 --> 00:16:12,100
and these little brown beads

619
00:16:12,100 --> 00:16:13,280
they represent iron.

620
00:16:13,500 --> 00:16:14,120
So there's iron

621
00:16:14,120 --> 00:16:15,760
depositing on this rod

622
00:16:15,760 --> 00:16:16,620
and this is also called

623
00:16:16,620 --> 00:16:17,980
a ferruginous body

624
00:16:17,980 --> 00:16:20,000
and so that's another name

625
00:16:20,000 --> 00:16:22,660
for this particular particle

626
00:16:22,660 --> 00:16:23,560
but essentially

627
00:16:23,560 --> 00:16:24,500
this represents

628
00:16:24,500 --> 00:16:26,100
asbestos within the patient

629
00:16:26,100 --> 00:16:27,860
and so that's a pathologic way

630
00:16:27,860 --> 00:16:28,960
by which we can confirm

631
00:16:28,960 --> 00:16:30,160
the fact that the patient

632
00:16:30,160 --> 00:16:31,460
is exposed to asbestos.

633
00:16:31,860 --> 00:16:32,580
So those are the four

634
00:16:32,580 --> 00:16:33,240
pneumoconiosis

635
00:16:33,240 --> 00:16:34,000
and I've told you

636
00:16:34,000 --> 00:16:34,640
what I think

637
00:16:34,640 --> 00:16:36,240
to be the highest yield

638
00:16:36,240 --> 00:16:37,420
for each of those

639
00:16:37,420 --> 00:16:38,760
individual pneumoconiosis.

640
00:16:39,840 --> 00:16:40,440
Sarcoidosis

641
00:16:40,440 --> 00:16:41,280
is another disease

642
00:16:41,280 --> 00:16:42,020
that can result

643
00:16:42,020 --> 00:16:42,940
in granulomas

644
00:16:42,940 --> 00:16:43,980
within the interstitium

645
00:16:43,980 --> 00:16:44,460
of the lung

646
00:16:44,460 --> 00:16:45,640
and those granulomas

647
00:16:45,640 --> 00:16:46,180
would result

648
00:16:46,180 --> 00:16:47,140
in restricted filling

649
00:16:47,140 --> 00:16:47,620
of the lung.

650
00:16:48,120 --> 00:16:49,360
Remember that sarcoidosis

651
00:16:49,360 --> 00:16:50,680
is a systemic disease

652
00:16:50,680 --> 00:16:51,480
characterized by

653
00:16:51,480 --> 00:16:52,880
non-caseating granulomas

654
00:16:52,880 --> 00:16:54,160
in multiple organs.

655
00:16:54,660 --> 00:16:55,480
The most commonly

656
00:16:55,480 --> 00:16:56,180
involved organs

657
00:16:56,180 --> 00:16:56,920
would be the lung

658
00:16:56,920 --> 00:16:58,080
and the hyalur lymph nodes

659
00:16:58,080 --> 00:16:59,520
as I'll highlight momentarily.

660
00:17:00,140 --> 00:17:00,960
Classically seen

661
00:17:00,960 --> 00:17:02,580
in African American females

662
00:17:02,580 --> 00:17:03,460
we don't know

663
00:17:03,460 --> 00:17:04,240
what causes it.

664
00:17:04,500 --> 00:17:05,060
It's probably

665
00:17:05,060 --> 00:17:06,520
some unknown antigen

666
00:17:06,520 --> 00:17:08,240
with a CD4 positive

667
00:17:08,240 --> 00:17:09,940
helper T cell response.

668
00:17:10,640 --> 00:17:11,700
Here's what the granulomas

669
00:17:11,700 --> 00:17:12,260
look like.

670
00:17:12,600 --> 00:17:13,540
Here I've illustrated

671
00:17:13,540 --> 00:17:13,980
for you

672
00:17:13,980 --> 00:17:14,840
this is the lung.

673
00:17:14,840 --> 00:17:16,060
There's an airspace here

674
00:17:16,060 --> 00:17:16,880
and then you've got

675
00:17:16,880 --> 00:17:18,320
this pink region here

676
00:17:18,320 --> 00:17:20,500
of epithelioid histiocytes.

677
00:17:20,660 --> 00:17:21,720
Remember that the defining

678
00:17:21,720 --> 00:17:22,860
cell of a granuloma

679
00:17:22,860 --> 00:17:24,680
is an epithelioid histiocyte.

680
00:17:25,000 --> 00:17:25,320
In addition

681
00:17:25,320 --> 00:17:25,900
you have some

682
00:17:25,900 --> 00:17:27,040
of the characteristic cells

683
00:17:27,040 --> 00:17:27,740
for example

684
00:17:27,740 --> 00:17:28,920
these giant cells.

685
00:17:29,380 --> 00:17:29,860
So this is

686
00:17:29,860 --> 00:17:30,880
the classic granuloma.

687
00:17:31,020 --> 00:17:32,040
It's non-caseating

688
00:17:32,040 --> 00:17:33,640
which means that

689
00:17:33,640 --> 00:17:34,620
all of the cells

690
00:17:34,620 --> 00:17:35,840
present within the granuloma

691
00:17:35,840 --> 00:17:36,560
are alive.

692
00:17:36,700 --> 00:17:37,840
There is no necrosis.

693
00:17:38,280 --> 00:17:39,220
One of the characteristic

694
00:17:39,220 --> 00:17:40,820
findings that can be seen

695
00:17:40,820 --> 00:17:41,640
in the granulomas

696
00:17:41,640 --> 00:17:43,000
of sarcoidosis

697
00:17:43,000 --> 00:17:44,020
is something called

698
00:17:44,020 --> 00:17:45,160
an asteroid body

699
00:17:45,160 --> 00:17:46,400
and this is what we mean

700
00:17:46,400 --> 00:17:47,340
by an asteroid body.

701
00:17:47,540 --> 00:17:48,920
It's just a funny

702
00:17:48,920 --> 00:17:50,180
configuration of some

703
00:17:50,180 --> 00:17:51,020
of the giant cells

704
00:17:51,020 --> 00:17:52,360
and it's one of the

705
00:17:52,360 --> 00:17:53,340
characteristic findings

706
00:17:53,340 --> 00:17:54,740
in sarcoidosis as well.

707
00:17:55,820 --> 00:17:56,540
The granulomas

708
00:17:56,540 --> 00:17:57,080
as I've said

709
00:17:57,080 --> 00:17:58,180
they most commonly involve

710
00:17:58,180 --> 00:17:59,180
the hyalur lymph node

711
00:17:59,180 --> 00:17:59,660
in the lung.

712
00:18:00,040 --> 00:18:00,900
Involvement of the lung

713
00:18:00,900 --> 00:18:02,280
is going to then create

714
00:18:02,280 --> 00:18:05,220
an interstitial problem

715
00:18:05,220 --> 00:18:06,680
and that interstitial problem

716
00:18:06,680 --> 00:18:08,040
will lead to a

717
00:18:08,040 --> 00:18:09,240
restrictive lung disease.

718
00:18:09,380 --> 00:18:10,380
Basically the lung

719
00:18:10,380 --> 00:18:11,680
becomes less compliant

720
00:18:11,680 --> 00:18:13,020
due to all of the

721
00:18:13,020 --> 00:18:14,340
granulomas present

722
00:18:14,340 --> 00:18:15,420
within the interstitium.

723
00:18:15,920 --> 00:18:16,980
Of course the granulomas

724
00:18:16,980 --> 00:18:17,520
can involve

725
00:18:17,520 --> 00:18:18,840
multiple organs as well.

726
00:18:19,160 --> 00:18:20,200
So if it involves the eye

727
00:18:20,200 --> 00:18:21,100
you get uveitis.

728
00:18:21,560 --> 00:18:22,940
If it involves the skin

729
00:18:22,940 --> 00:18:24,700
you can get cutaneous nodules.

730
00:18:25,140 --> 00:18:25,740
It can involve

731
00:18:25,740 --> 00:18:26,640
the salivary glands

732
00:18:26,640 --> 00:18:28,140
and the lacrimal glands

733
00:18:28,140 --> 00:18:28,900
so it can mimic

734
00:18:28,900 --> 00:18:29,640
Sjogren's syndrome

735
00:18:29,640 --> 00:18:30,600
and this is very important

736
00:18:30,600 --> 00:18:31,700
because again it's sort of

737
00:18:31,700 --> 00:18:32,820
the knee jerk questions

738
00:18:32,820 --> 00:18:33,740
that show up on exams.

739
00:18:34,140 --> 00:18:34,880
They expect you to

740
00:18:34,880 --> 00:18:35,740
expect you to jump

741
00:18:35,740 --> 00:18:36,520
for Sjogren's syndrome

742
00:18:36,520 --> 00:18:37,180
but actually

743
00:18:37,180 --> 00:18:38,680
they're talking about

744
00:18:38,680 --> 00:18:39,340
something different

745
00:18:39,340 --> 00:18:39,980
and in this case

746
00:18:39,980 --> 00:18:40,860
they're talking about

747
00:18:40,860 --> 00:18:41,900
sarcoidosis.

748
00:18:42,340 --> 00:18:42,940
So just remember

749
00:18:42,940 --> 00:18:43,780
that it can involve

750
00:18:43,780 --> 00:18:44,580
the salivary glands

751
00:18:44,580 --> 00:18:45,340
and lacrimal glands

752
00:18:45,340 --> 00:18:46,320
giving you the classic

753
00:18:46,320 --> 00:18:47,420
doc I can't chew

754
00:18:47,420 --> 00:18:48,040
a cracker

755
00:18:48,040 --> 00:18:49,980
and there's dirt in my eyes

756
00:18:49,980 --> 00:18:50,940
and an increased risk

757
00:18:50,940 --> 00:18:51,780
of dental caries

758
00:18:51,780 --> 00:18:52,640
those are the classic

759
00:18:52,640 --> 00:18:53,520
clinical findings

760
00:18:53,520 --> 00:18:54,780
in Sjogren's syndrome

761
00:18:54,780 --> 00:18:56,220
and so you could actually

762
00:18:56,220 --> 00:18:56,940
do a biopsy

763
00:18:56,940 --> 00:18:58,300
and see non-caseating

764
00:18:58,300 --> 00:18:58,940
granulomas

765
00:18:58,940 --> 00:18:59,420
and if you have

766
00:18:59,420 --> 00:19:00,280
non-caseating

767
00:19:00,280 --> 00:19:00,940
granulomas

768
00:19:00,940 --> 00:19:01,820
with those symptoms

769
00:19:01,820 --> 00:19:03,780
that is sarcoidosis

770
00:19:03,780 --> 00:19:05,200
that's classic

771
00:19:05,200 --> 00:19:06,080
for sarcoidosis

772
00:19:06,080 --> 00:19:06,580
I should say

773
00:19:06,580 --> 00:19:07,260
and again

774
00:19:07,260 --> 00:19:07,960
any tissue

775
00:19:07,960 --> 00:19:09,060
can almost any tissue

776
00:19:09,060 --> 00:19:10,000
can really be involved

777
00:19:10,000 --> 00:19:11,120
I've just told you

778
00:19:11,120 --> 00:19:11,680
a couple of the

779
00:19:11,680 --> 00:19:12,720
high yield associations.

780
00:19:13,840 --> 00:19:14,620
Now the way

781
00:19:14,620 --> 00:19:15,260
that these patients

782
00:19:15,260 --> 00:19:16,300
present is

783
00:19:16,300 --> 00:19:17,480
the most common sign

784
00:19:17,480 --> 00:19:18,120
is cough

785
00:19:18,120 --> 00:19:19,180
but they can also

786
00:19:19,180 --> 00:19:20,260
have shortness of breath

787
00:19:20,260 --> 00:19:20,940
due to that

788
00:19:20,940 --> 00:19:22,460
restrictive lung disease

789
00:19:22,460 --> 00:19:23,080
that's going to be

790
00:19:23,080 --> 00:19:24,680
created by the sarcoid.

791
00:19:25,400 --> 00:19:26,640
Another very important

792
00:19:26,640 --> 00:19:27,100
finding is

793
00:19:30,280 --> 00:19:31,280
angiotensin converting

794
00:19:31,280 --> 00:19:31,740
enzyme

795
00:19:31,740 --> 00:19:32,860
can be elevated

796
00:19:32,860 --> 00:19:33,460
in the blood

797
00:19:33,460 --> 00:19:34,620
the patients have

798
00:19:34,620 --> 00:19:35,540
hypercalcemia

799
00:19:35,540 --> 00:19:36,280
this is important

800
00:19:36,280 --> 00:19:37,100
I'd like to ask you

801
00:19:37,100 --> 00:19:37,420
why.

802
00:19:38,060 --> 00:19:39,240
So the hypercalcemia

803
00:19:39,240 --> 00:19:40,120
occurs because

804
00:19:40,120 --> 00:19:41,400
the granulomas

805
00:19:41,400 --> 00:19:42,900
have one alpha

806
00:19:42,900 --> 00:19:44,040
hydroxylase activity

807
00:19:44,040 --> 00:19:45,260
and they can activate

808
00:19:45,260 --> 00:19:45,920
vitamin D.

809
00:19:46,460 --> 00:19:47,720
Now although we

810
00:19:47,720 --> 00:19:48,900
classically apply this

811
00:19:48,900 --> 00:19:49,500
to sarcoid

812
00:19:49,500 --> 00:19:50,140
and say because

813
00:19:50,140 --> 00:19:50,700
they're activating

814
00:19:50,700 --> 00:19:51,380
vitamin D

815
00:19:51,380 --> 00:19:52,160
there's going to be

816
00:19:52,160 --> 00:19:53,020
hypercalcemia

817
00:19:53,020 --> 00:19:54,420
in any disease

818
00:19:54,420 --> 00:19:55,180
in which the patients

819
00:19:55,180 --> 00:19:56,280
have a ton of

820
00:19:56,280 --> 00:19:57,480
non-caseating granulomas

821
00:19:57,480 --> 00:19:58,060
for example

822
00:19:58,060 --> 00:19:58,860
there will be

823
00:19:58,860 --> 00:20:00,820
excess activity

824
00:20:00,820 --> 00:20:01,540
of the one alpha

825
00:20:01,540 --> 00:20:02,300
hydroxylase

826
00:20:02,300 --> 00:20:03,000
which will then

827
00:20:03,000 --> 00:20:04,600
result in

828
00:20:04,600 --> 00:20:05,320
the production

829
00:20:05,320 --> 00:20:06,280
of hypercalcemia.

830
00:20:06,660 --> 00:20:07,200
So for example

831
00:20:07,200 --> 00:20:07,660
if a patient

832
00:20:07,660 --> 00:20:08,440
was exposed to

833
00:20:08,440 --> 00:20:09,000
beryllium

834
00:20:09,000 --> 00:20:09,540
and developed

835
00:20:09,540 --> 00:20:10,300
a very similar

836
00:20:10,300 --> 00:20:11,280
picture to sarcoid

837
00:20:11,280 --> 00:20:12,240
and they also have

838
00:20:12,240 --> 00:20:13,060
hypercalcemia

839
00:20:13,060 --> 00:20:13,760
that's okay

840
00:20:13,760 --> 00:20:14,380
because it's

841
00:20:14,380 --> 00:20:15,420
the non-caseating

842
00:20:15,420 --> 00:20:16,020
granuloma

843
00:20:16,020 --> 00:20:16,940
that actually has

844
00:20:16,940 --> 00:20:17,920
the alpha one

845
00:20:17,920 --> 00:20:18,980
hydroxylase activity

846
00:20:18,980 --> 00:20:19,860
that's resulting

847
00:20:19,860 --> 00:20:20,440
in that

848
00:20:20,440 --> 00:20:22,020
hypercalcemia.

849
00:20:22,020 --> 00:20:23,280
The treatment is steroids

850
00:20:23,280 --> 00:20:24,260
but what's interesting

851
00:20:24,260 --> 00:20:25,000
is that often

852
00:20:25,000 --> 00:20:25,640
this disease

853
00:20:25,640 --> 00:20:26,220
will resolve

854
00:20:26,220 --> 00:20:26,900
spontaneously

855
00:20:26,900 --> 00:20:28,220
without treatment.

856
00:20:29,220 --> 00:20:29,980
The final

857
00:20:29,980 --> 00:20:30,760
restrictive disease

858
00:20:30,760 --> 00:20:31,780
is hypersensitivity

859
00:20:31,780 --> 00:20:32,300
pneumonitis

860
00:20:32,300 --> 00:20:33,340
and the idea

861
00:20:33,340 --> 00:20:34,260
here is that

862
00:20:34,260 --> 00:20:34,840
a patient

863
00:20:34,840 --> 00:20:35,480
gets exposed

864
00:20:35,480 --> 00:20:36,160
to some sort

865
00:20:36,160 --> 00:20:36,820
of inhaled

866
00:20:36,820 --> 00:20:37,940
organic antigen

867
00:20:37,940 --> 00:20:38,620
it could be

868
00:20:38,620 --> 00:20:39,100
for example

869
00:20:39,100 --> 00:20:39,660
the feces

870
00:20:39,660 --> 00:20:40,320
of a bird

871
00:20:40,320 --> 00:20:41,160
or sometimes

872
00:20:41,160 --> 00:20:41,660
feathers

873
00:20:41,660 --> 00:20:42,060
etc.

874
00:20:42,060 --> 00:20:43,180
and that results

875
00:20:43,180 --> 00:20:44,100
in a granulomatous

876
00:20:44,100 --> 00:20:45,020
reaction to that

877
00:20:45,020 --> 00:20:45,560
antigen.

878
00:20:46,100 --> 00:20:46,540
Now when there's

879
00:20:46,540 --> 00:20:47,160
a granulomatous

880
00:20:47,160 --> 00:20:47,780
reaction to that

881
00:20:47,780 --> 00:20:48,100
antigen

882
00:20:48,100 --> 00:20:48,560
the patients

883
00:20:48,560 --> 00:20:48,940
will present

884
00:20:48,940 --> 00:20:49,480
with fever

885
00:20:49,480 --> 00:20:50,180
